Through years of striking hard surfaces and specialized conditioning exercises,
monks following the Iron Body path develop hands that strike with the force
and durability of iron. The calluses, bone density, and tendon strength
achieved through this training transform bare fists into formidable weapons.

This passive skill provides a damage bonus of up to 8.3% when attacking with
bare hands. The bonus requires that both hands be ungloved - wearing any
hand equipment negates the iron fist advantage, as the conditioning relies
on direct contact between hardened flesh and target.

Iron Fist is the foundation of the Iron Body discipline, representing the
monk's first steps in hardening their physical form. The enhanced striking
power combines with other barehand bonuses to make a skilled monk's
unarmed attacks devastatingly effective.

The conditioning process is gradual but permanent. A monk who has trained
iron fist carries the benefits throughout their life, their hands bearing
the characteristic calluses and density of their dedication.

